--TEST--
`Rock::class as ?class<Animal>` is the same compile-time refusal the checked spelling is — `rule:types/class-reference` decides a written-out `::class` operand, so there is no run-time throw for `rule:expressions/nullable-conversion-availability`'s `?` to answer `null` for
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {}
class Rock {}
?class<Animal> $c = Rock::class as ?class<Animal>;
echo $c == null ? "null" : "set", "\n";
